    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d911">

                <pb facs="1077" n="1061" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg1061"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">831.00/9–1247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Maleady</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-09-12T10:00:00-04:30">September 12,
                            1947—10 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>363. All Caracas barracks and those La Guaira area alerted early this a.m., as
                    were presumably all others throughout country. Traffic being rerouted in all
                    streets adjacent Caracas <hi rendition="#italic">cuartels</hi>. Military guards
                    are dressed full equipment. Radio stations under guard. Armored and other
                    military cars in evidence all downtown streets. Approximately twelve well-known
                    civilians including Director Geology in Ministry of Fomento, Victor Lopez,
                    arrested.</p>
                <p>Some informants state show military force made intentionally by administration in
                    Junta to impress populace and prevent attempt break up meeting here at which
                        Gallegos’<anchor n="21" xml:id="d911-f1"/> presidential candidacy to be
                    publicly proclaimed tonight. Others feel alert occasioned by matter mentioned
                        mytel 361, September 11, 4 p.m.<anchor
                        n="22" xml:id="d911-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Reports of uprisings at various places outside Caracas wholly unconfirmed.</p>
                <p>Miraflores Palace source states situation under control and has promised furnish
                    me full details this noon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Maleady</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d911-f1" n="21" xml:id="d911-f1-content">
                <p>Romulo Gallegos, candidate of the governing Junta.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d911-f2" n="22" xml:id="d911-f2-content">
